[{"url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@dimonplaypro42/video/7698803974597610760", "post_id": "7698803974597610760", "description": "Genetics determines many aspects of our appearance, such as eye color, hair color, skin tone, height, facial features, and body structure. We inherit genes from both parents, which influence how we look.#lookism #genetics\nExplore how genes from both parents shape eye color, hair, skin tone, height, facial features and body structure. Clear, concise genetics explanation. #lookism #genetics\nGenetics shapes many visible traits: eye color, hair color, skin tone, height, facial features, and overall body structure. Each of these characteristics is influenced by the combination of genes inherited from both parents.\n\nGenes and inheritance\n- Every person inherits two copies of most genes — one from each parent. Variations in those genes (alleles) interact to produce visible traits.\n- Some traits follow simple patterns (dominant vs. recessive alleles), while most appearance traits are polygenic, meaning many genes contribute small effects.\n\nEye color and hair color\n- Eye color depends on genes that affect pigment production and distribution in the iris. Multiple genes interact to create the range from blue to brown and intermediate shades.\n- Hair color is influenced by pigment genes and can vary with multiple interacting genes that determine eumelanin and pheomelanin levels.\n\nSkin tone\n- Skin color is strongly polygenic. Several genes influence how much melanin the skin produces and how it’s distributed, producing a continuum of skin tones rather than discrete categories.\n\nHeight and body structure\n- Height is highly polygenic: hundreds of genes contribute small effects, combined with nutrition and environment. Body proportions and skeletal structure also reflect many genetic influences plus developmental factors.\n\nFacial features\n- Shape of the nose, jawline, cheekbones, and other facial traits result from many genes that control growth patterns and tissue development. These combine with environmental and developmental influences to produce unique faces.\n\nVariation and environment\n- Genetics sets a blueprint, but environment matters. Nutrition, health during development, sun exposure, and aging all interact with genes to shape appearance over a lifetime.\n\nTakeaway\n- Appearance is the result of complex inheritances: some traits follow simple genetic rules, but most are polygenic with contributions from many genes and environmental factors. We inherit a mix from both parents that together produce individual looks.\n\nEngagement prompt\n- Which inherited trait do you notice most in your family? Share an example of a feature that runs in your relatives. \n", "create_time": "2026-10-20T17:31:32.000Z", "digg_count": 36500, "share_count": "2410", "collect_count": 5729, "comment_count": 109, "play_count": 244200, "video_duration": 18, "hashtags": ["lookism", "genetics"], "original_sound": "atlantics: original sound", "profile_id": "6676658446065320965", "profile_username": "voley", "profile_url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@dimonplaypro42", "profile_avatar": "https://p16-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-alisg-avt-0068/9e0082fc144a09c10d276ce289595984~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:1080:1080.jpeg?dr=9640&refresh_token=721ad35c&x-expires=1795989600&x-signature=WWIUPbJlQMwXMnQQemAQHe8Mblw%3D&t=4d5b0474&ps=13740610&shp=a5d48078&shcp=81f88b70&idc=useast5", "profile_biography": "No bio yet", "preview_image": "https://p19-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-alisg-p-0037/ocB4Oq6BgfREEaFRH2IA2SAQ7pgf9i5XrL1EXD~tplv-tiktokx-origin.image?dr=9636&x-expires=1795989600&x-signature=7SDIbPR9GPywOUq%2BhDUufRwCEDs%3D&t=4d5b0474&ps=13740610&shp=81f88b70&shcp=43f4a2f9&idc=useast5", "post_type": "video", "discovery_input": {"url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@dimonplaypro42", "num_of_posts": 40, "start_date": "", "end_date": "", "what_to_collect": "", "post_type": "", "country": "", "sort_by": ""}, "offical_item": false, "secu_id"